===============================
PDF → PROFILE ARCHITECTURE (MVP)
===============================

1. OVERVIEW FLOW

Client (Frontend)
    ↓
POST /api/profile/upload-resume
    ↓
Upload Controller (Backend)
    ↓
File Processing Layer
    ↓
PDF Text Extraction (pdf-parse)
    ↓
Text Preprocessing
    ↓
LLM Parsing Service
    ↓
Validation + Normalization
    ↓
UserProfile DB (Postgres)
    ↓
Response → Editable Profile


--------------------------------
2. END-TO-END FLOW
--------------------------------

1. User uploads resume (PDF)
2. Backend receives file (multipart/form-data)
3. Extract raw text from PDF
4. Clean + preprocess text
5. Send to LLM with structured prompt
6. Receive JSON response
7. Validate JSON structure
8. Normalize fields
9. Store in UserProfile table
10. Return profile to frontend
11. User edits (optional) → save


--------------------------------
3. API DESIGN
--------------------------------

POST /api/profile/upload-resume

Request:
- multipart/form-data
- file: resume.pdf

Response:
{
  "profile": { ... },
  "editable": true
}


--------------------------------
4. COMPONENTS
--------------------------------

A. Upload Controller
- Validate file type (PDF)
- Validate size (max 5MB)
- Pass file buffer to service

B. File Processing Layer
- Handles file buffer
- No storage (MVP)

C. PDF Extraction Service
- Use pdf-parse
- Output: raw text string

D. Preprocessing Layer
- Remove extra spaces
- Remove special characters
- Trim long text

E. LLM Parsing Service
- Input: cleaned resume text
- Output: structured JSON

F. Validation Layer
- Check required fields
- Ensure valid JSON

G. Normalization Layer
- Lowercase skills
- Remove duplicates
- Standardize roles

H. Database Layer
- Store structured profile

I. Response Layer
- Return editable profile


--------------------------------
5. DATABASE SCHEMA
--------------------------------

Table: UserProfile

{
  user_id: string,

  name: string,
  email: string,
  phone: string,

  experience_years: number,
  current_role: string,
  seniority_level: string,

  skills: string[],
  technologies: string[],

  past_companies: string[],
  education: string,

  projects_summary: string,
  resume_summary: string,

  tags: string[],

  updated_at: timestamp
}


--------------------------------
6. RE-UPLOAD FLOW
--------------------------------

if (user uploads new resume):
    parse again
    overwrite existing profile
    update timestamp


--------------------------------
7. ERROR HANDLING
--------------------------------

Case 1: PDF parse fails
→ return error: "Unable to read resume"

Case 2: LLM fails
→ retry once

Case 3: Invalid JSON
→ re-prompt LLM to fix format


--------------------------------
8. PERFORMANCE (MVP)
--------------------------------

- Keep synchronous processing
- LLM timeout: 10–15 seconds
- Optimize text before sending


--------------------------------
9. SECURITY
--------------------------------

- Allow only PDF files
- Limit file size (2–5 MB)
- Sanitize inputs
- Do NOT store raw files


--------------------------------
10. FUTURE EXTENSIONS
--------------------------------

- Add S3 storage (optional)
- Async processing (queue + worker)
- Profile versioning
- Confidence score
- Missing fields detection


--------------------------------
11. KEY PRINCIPLES
--------------------------------

- No file storage (MVP)
- Store only structured data
- Keep pipeline simple
- Ensure clean JSON output
- Allow user edits